comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-17T22:03:34.213Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete live 2766-item all-status export has no omissions; request-specific packed and command_finish searches plus title/description comparison found no owner for the first-request collector assumption. Reuse the shipped acceptance lineage through verifies; original acceptance and telemetry completion fixes remain closed. Failure: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/35278617240/job/105395397463."
  "2026-09-17T22:06:09.137Z","harness:codex","TDD reproduced the hosted failure through two real HTTP requests: the extracted existing once-request collector rejected the first command_start batch with the same command_finish assertion. The collector now consumes bounded request events until completion, acknowledges every batch, and removes listeners on success or deadline. Physical queue and successful-flush assertions remain unchanged. Also documented the three previously undocumented named test helpers from the reviewed tranche."
  "2026-09-17T22:07:45.742Z","harness:codex","Review disposition: CodeRabbit full review of 66af0f4ec reported minimal risk and no actionable code findings. Its baseline scope warning is declined: the first-class omission receipt requires four measured tokens in compact next output; the generated full corpus decreases six tokens overall, with unchanged enforcement and a passing seeded regression control. The new collector fix additionally aborts stalled request bodies under the same 30-second deadline and tests listener cleanup after success and timeout."
  "2026-09-17T22:19:50.879Z","harness:codex","Verification complete: real split-request completion, absent completion, incomplete request-body timeout and listener-cleanup controls pass; linked packed acceptance passes. Full suite passes 8975 tests across 704 files with exact coverage 64768/64768 statements, 49409/49409 branches, 13443/13443 functions and 61997/61997 lines. Fresh npm/Bun installations pass SDK/CLI/MCP/npx/bunx/lifecycle and the corrected detached telemetry collector with physical queue-drain proof. Timeout, completion requirement and installed-artifact assertions were retained."
  "2026-09-17T22:29:35.945Z","harness:codex","Final static and type gates pass after closure, including mandatory defect evidence and unchanged graph/record-integrity bounds. Live telemetry correlation for 2026-09-17 22:10-22:20 UTC matched 38 starts to exactly one finish using installation/session/command and finish.started_at versus start.occurred_at; zero missing or duplicate finishes. Broker ready and unacknowledged queues were both zero. This bounded cohort is separate from the real isolated packed collector proof and is not a claim about all historical events."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-17T22:19:51.492Z","harness:codex","A telemetry transport request is a batch boundary, not a command-completion boundary. Acceptance must acknowledge start-only batches and await actual completion under one deadline, including request-body reads; missing completion must still fail."
